\strong{Utilization level.} These convert whole-stem volume of trees with
\verb{Dbh >= 4.0 cm} to biomass of trees with \verb{Dbh >= 4.0 cm}. Pairing them with
volume compiled at any other utilization level pairs volumes with the wrong
conversion; the FAIB ground-plot compilations record this as \code{UTIL}, and
\code{\link[=assemble_faib_ground_plots]{assemble_faib_ground_plots()}} filters to \code{UTIL == 4} for exactly this
reason. The source report also publishes factors for the 7.5, 12.5, 17.5 and
22.5 cm levels, which are NOT included here.

\strong{Units.} Volume is m^3 ha^-1 and biomass is tonnes ha^-1, i.e. oven-dry
mass. To get CARBON, apply a carbon fraction yourself -- the coefficients do
not include one.

\strong{Coverage.} All 16 species groups x 14 BEC zones are populated, with no
gaps. Where the report had too little data to fit a (group, zone) stratum it
fell back to that group pooled over all zones, so a value being present is
not on its own evidence that it was fitted on local data. Judge that with
\link{kivari_sample_frequency} and \link{kivari_correlation}.
